shapes, the ship, the band and every effect are drawn at runtime by this
project's own code.

games/blast-maze/ awarded 10 points per soft block and 200 per enemy, close
enough to the arcade bomb-maze table to be worth changing. The values are now
15 per crate, 250 per enemy, 60 per power-up and 400 plus 80 per level for
clearing the maze. The green field and brown bricks were replaced by the
collection's palette - indigo floor, steel pillars, amber crates, a pink
player orb and violet enemies. Neither game names, nor borrows art or code
from, any other product; "Bug Column" and "Blast Maze" are this project's own
titles, as are the folder names, the ids and the i18n prefixes.

The third game of the batch, games/orbit-escape/, needed no licensing change:
the name, the id, the prefix, the gravity wells, the debris, the fuel cells and
the exit portal are all this project's own, and its scoring (4 points per
second of flight, 200 plus 60 per level plus 2 per percent of fuel left at the
portal, 40 per fuel cell) was invented for it. The word on the portal is now
translated instead of the hardcoded English "EXIT".

